A few things I learned as I now have an ascendable Monk (sitting on
the Plane of Air currently):

1)  Your pet is very important early - Since you can't hit the broad
side of a barn with body armor early, your pet is essential to
detecting cursed armor early since you'll be trying on just about
every piece of armor you find.  Also, your pet keeps you from getting
surrounded and over your head early.

2)  Reflection - It's always big, but possibly more so for Monks.  You
don't have the benefit of high HPs or low AC, so make sure you get it
early.

3)  ? of Enchant Armor - Use everyone you find.  Due to the armor
limits, you need to maximize every piece of armor you get.

4)  Robe - Depending which way you opt to go CoMR or Robe, make sure
you fireproof your your Robe early because you can't get another one
easily.

5)  Hoard food early.  I wound up violating my vegan conduct
accidentally, but food was beginning to become a nuisance until I
found Fort Ludios.

Sure, some of this is self-explanatory/good play any way, but these
become much more prominant for a monk.


